<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36135" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">phōnascus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνασκός</span>
		(singing-master; hence), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A teacher of singing and declamation</i>: phonascus
			assum vocis suscitabulum, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 176,
				30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 23</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dare operam phonasco,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Aug. 84</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3,
			22</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A musical director</i>, <i>chorister</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psalmorum hic modulator et phonascus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
